{:edb/db-before-t 840 :edb/db-after-t 841 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534153 50 #inst "2026-10-06T05:25:11.024Z" 13194139534153 true] [17592186100791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279103 13194139534153 true] [17592186100791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279110 13194139534153 true] [17592186100791 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279113 13194139534153 true] [17592186100792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279117 13194139534153 true] [17592186100792 1020 #edb/ref 17592186279120 13194139534153 true] [17592186279103 1017 #edb/ref 17592186279104 13194139534153 true] [17592186279103 1089 "q-13953" 13194139534153 true] [17592186279103 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534153 true] [17592186279103 1100 "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534153 true] [17592186279103 1113 #uuid "7865cd6e-ceef-559e-ad51-f022571355c8" 13194139534153 true] [17592186279103 1145 "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,6\\,|=6\n$$" 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279105 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279106 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279107 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279108 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279109 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1041 "selection" 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279106 13194139534153 true] [17592186279104 1110 #uuid "942e7e44-d688-53e6-a3f6-4fcaecb18